      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T21:49:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like you always use `__rmqueue_pcplist_cma()` in combination with `__rmqueue_pcplist()` (as a fallback). Why not implement this logic inside `__rmqueue_pcplist()`? You could rename current `__rmqueue_pcplist()` into `___rmqueue_pcplist()` and then have:\n```\n__rmqueue_pcplist(...)\n{\n    if (cma_fallback_restricted() \u0026\u0026 alloc_flags \u0026 ALLOC_CMA) {\n        struct page *page;\n        struct list_head *cmalist;\n        cmalist \u003d \u0026pcp-\u003elists[order_to_pindex(migratetype, order)];\n        page \u003d ___rmqueue_pcplist(zone, order, get_cma_migrate_type(),\n\t\t\t\t\t alloc_flags, pcp, cmalist);\n        if (page) return page;\n    }\n    return ___rmqueue_pcplist(zone, order, migratetype, alloc_flags,\n\t\t\t\t\t pcp, list);\n}\n```\nThis way you don\u0027t need code changes at the call sites in `rmqueue_pcplist` and `__alloc_pages_bulk`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2777,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 2777,
        "endChar": 41
      },
